# 詞: 銀包

1. 我唔見咗個銀包，而家好徬徨。 (I've lost my wallet, and I'm feeling really anxious now.)

2. 佢個銀包入面有好多張信用卡，唔見咗就大鑊。 (He has a lot of credit cards in his wallet. If he loses it, it's a big problem.)

3. 你記得帶銀包出街呀，唔好又漏咗喺屋企。 (Remember to bring your wallet when you go out. Don't leave it at home again.)

4. 我個銀包舊咗，想買個新嘅送畀自己。 (My wallet is old. I want to buy a new one for myself.)

5. 佢打開個銀包，發現入面得一張一百蚊紙。 (He opened his wallet and found only a hundred-dollar bill inside.)

6. 唔好成日將個銀包放喺褲後袋，好易俾人偷。 (Don't always put your wallet in your back pocket. It's easy for thieves to steal it.)

7. 我個銀包係女朋友送嘅，所以好有紀念價值。 (My wallet was a gift from my girlfriend, so it has a lot of sentimental value.)

8. 佢喺街度執到個銀包，即刻交咗去警署。 (He found a wallet on the street and immediately handed it in to the police station.)

9. 我銀包入面啲散紙成日跌晒出嚟，好麻煩。 (The loose change in my wallet keeps falling out all the time. It's really annoying.)

10. 你睇吓你個銀包，塞到脹卜卜，係時候清理吓喇。 (Look at your wallet – it's stuffed so full. It's time to clean it out.) [end of text]


